cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the velurex encoding in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Quintrit"
abstract: "Ternary-weight inference with velurex encoding: five trits per byte (1.60 bits per weight), exact SIMD kernels for AVX2, AVX-512 and NEON, a GGUF reader and a transformer runtime, with C, C++ and Python bindings."
authors:
  - family-names: "Velecký"
    given-names: "Lukáš"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/velurex-labs/quintrit"
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - ternary quantization
  - velurex encoding
  - SIMD
  - LLM inference
  - GGUF
